WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.190
We're at a historic
tipping point for women.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.119
In October 2017,

00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:15.020
the #MeToo

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.453
spread across the globe.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.830
What began as a Hollywood
sexual assault scandal

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.203
sparked a public reckoning
around the world.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.710
Thousands of women are using two words

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.160
on social media to identify themselves

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.400
as survivors of sexual
harassment and assault.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.690
A watershed moment in our--

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.430
New laws have been passed

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.910
and powerful men have
been forced to step down.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.523
We are sorry

00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:46.360
for the damage that Oxfam has done.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.610
Face arrest and conviction.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:53.330
But now MeToo is igniting wider debates.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.943
A new day is on the horizon.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.689
About the ability of

00:00:57.689 --> 00:00:59.520
legal systems to deliver justice.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.737
The problem here is

00:01:00.737 --> 00:01:01.970
our systems are not strong
enough to back them.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.090
About how men should behave around women.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.190
We don't know what the rules are

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.750
and it turns out that there's way more

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.140
of them than you thought.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.770
And about the battle for gender equality.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.680
First you had MeToo

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.020
and now you have NowWhat.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.870
Pretoria, South Africa.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.580
Inspired by the global MeToo movement,

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.620
these women are protesting
about the country's

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.080
high rates of rape and femicide,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.823
the deliberate murder of women.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.880
In South Africa, the
number of women killed

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.940
by a partner or family
member is five times

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.723
higher than the global average.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.053
I would like to officially welcome

00:01:58.053 --> 00:01:59.533
each and every woman here.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.600
Avelafay is one of the organizers.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.700
Like many of the protestors, Avela

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.050
has been personally affected by femicide.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.270
At the age of 13 I lost
my mother to femicide.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.770
She was brutally murdered in her own home,

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.510
and the perpetrators are free,

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:27.760
they're roaming the streets.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.330
So, not only was I failed by
someone we knew as a family,

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.380
but we were failed by the justice system.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.820
Here, even a recent president, Jacob Zuma,

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.403
has been accused of rape.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.360
The charges were dropped in court in 2006.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.030
But sexual and physical violence

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.043
have continued to afflict
all levels of society.

00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:54.210
No means no, no means no--

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.750
Today the protestors are marching

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:58.010
on the parliament and
have demanded a hearing

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.353
with the current
president, Cyril Ramaphosa.

00:03:08.498 --> 00:03:12.260
But at the parliament buildings

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.313
it's soon clear the president
will not be meeting them.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.440
The president's no show
is little surprise.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.740
In this country the police
reported a 7.4% increase

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.563
in all crimes against women
in the last year alone.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.850
But for the protestors, today has still

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:48.903
been an important step in
raising public awareness.

00:04:09.007 --> 00:04:11.070
In Johannesburg, GiGI White

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.840
runs the charity Get Up Women.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.130
She helps victims of sexual violence

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:18.610
who's cases have been
dropped by the police.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.120
We're off to go and meet two ladies

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.803
who have allegedly been
raped by their boss.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.749
Nearly half of all rape cases reported

00:04:28.749 --> 00:04:33.483
to South African police do
not result in an arrest.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:41.800
Okay so before we start--

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.280
These two women allege

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.140
their boss sexually
assaulted them at work.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.990
We have got everybody and everything

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.810
it's going to take to keep you guys safe.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.270
Gigi has come with her colleagues

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.620
Sean and Dave to take
statements from them.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.170
So he just wants to ask
a couple of questions.

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.570
We have to do this properly.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.160
Sean's role is to pass evidence

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.530
to the police and pressure them

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.343
to investigate the case properly.

00:05:32.249 --> 00:05:34.166
Scooch up, scooch up.

00:05:35.657 --> 00:05:38.074
Come here my dear, come here.

00:06:07.121 --> 00:06:08.454
When was this?

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.920
The women suspect their boss

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.533
bribed the police to
drop the investigation.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.620
He doesn't know enough people, trust me.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.873
He's gonna need to know a
lot more after this one.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.380
And we will go through the
whole entire thing with you.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.960
Every case, every court
appearance we will be there.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.160
You will not do this alone.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:45.260
I think this is gonna be a lot uglier

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.970
and a lot bigger than
what we first thought.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.090
As a third woman has now said

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.510
she was assaulted by the same boss,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.190
Gigi hopes the police can be pushed

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.970
to re-open this case.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:01.130
But things could hit
a familiar brick wall.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.940
One of the biggest issues
that we have are the cops.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.570
Everybody's prepared to take a bribe.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.900
The number of women asking

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.170
Gigi for help has increased since MeToo.

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:13.400
Yet she's worried there
will be no lasting impact

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.020
in South Africa unless
there are more prosecutions.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.550
We have this huge, big
movement that started.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:21.150
Woman are getting out,
they're telling people

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.117
exactly what happened and how it happened.

00:07:23.117 --> 00:07:24.880
And the problem here is our systems

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.513
are not strong enough to back them.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.420
If we don't start getting
the prosecution done

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.180
and getting these women justice

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.423
we're just gonna end up sliding backwards.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.940
In America the MeToo movement

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.020
is starting to have an
impact on the justice system.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.635
A new day is on the horizon!

00:07:47.635 --> 00:07:49.510
Following the Harvey Weinstein scandal

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.870
over 300 public figures have
donated millions of dollars

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.632
to the Time's Up legal defense fund.

00:07:54.632 --> 00:07:58.860
Women have united to
claim that Time Is Up.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.460
At these small unassuming

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.840
head quarters in Washington, DC,

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.020
giant steps are being taken.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:09.948
We've got farm workers,
retail, hotel workers,

00:08:09.948 --> 00:08:12.670
nail salons, poultry workers--

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.250
American women can apply

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.680
to the fund for free legal support,

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.220
if they have been sexually harassed

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.533
or assaulted at work.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:25.220
So far there have been
over 3,500 applications.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.693
Mainly from women in low wage industries.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:30.493
Could I get your first and last--

00:08:30.493 --> 00:08:32.090
It's up to interns like Noah

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:34.370
to field the rising number of calls.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:36.300
These are the list of intakes that

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.370
we're gonna be sending attorneys to.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.150
We have it listed as
workplace sexual harassment

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:42.730
other workplace sex discrimination.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:46.480
There is probably at least 30
or 40 here, just for today.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:49.900
Some of the claims stretch back decades.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:52.538
The most memorable case I had to deal

00:08:52.538 --> 00:08:54.550
with was a woman in the military.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:57.140
She was sexually harassed
by her superiors,

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:02.050
by the people around her and
it kind of destroyed her life.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.367
She told me, "you're the first
person I ever told this to".

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.630
Applications vetted here

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.630
in Washington, DC are passed through

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.773
a network of 700 lawyers
working across 48 states.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:18.250
The fund has already filed
claims against McDonald's,

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.270
the U.S. postal service and Walmart.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.720
They hope this will prompt
other major organizations

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:26.840
to change their own rules
about sexual harassment.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.120
Employers have an opportunity
to lead right now.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.120
They don't actually need to
wait for new laws to pass.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.830
They can, right now, today decide

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:36.930
that they're gonna put this issue

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.863
at the center of their organization.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.260
MeToo has prompted some
companies in the west

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:48.403
to introduce new measures to
deal with sexual harassment.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:53.680
But it has also provoked an
all to predicable backlash.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:56.290
I've seen signs of kind of panic

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.650
around sexuality and particularly

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:01.250
a tendency to vilify all men.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.925
People are not actually going
through any court process--

00:10:03.925 --> 00:10:06.933
We're risking a kind of
social media lynching.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.640
Some of the backlash is being fueled

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:11.500
by the anxieties of men forced

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.000
to think about their behavior

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.230
in ways they never had to before.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:17.020
Well everyone always feels uncomfortable

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:19.060
when they don't know what the rules are.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.420
And now we don't know what the rules are.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.330
And it turns out that
there's way more of them

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.790
than you thought and that the punishment

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.940
for transgressing against
them is way higher

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.480
than you could have imagined.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.590
Clinical psychologist Jordan Peterson

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.030
is known for his controversial

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.333
and extremely devicive fuse on gender.

00:10:36.455 --> 00:10:37.288
You agree that it's unfair?

00:10:37.288 --> 00:10:39.320
If you're a woman--
Not necessarily.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.153
He's one of the most

00:10:40.153 --> 00:10:42.773
vocal critics of Me Too and its impact.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.570
The whole purpose in some sense

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.970
of the MeToo movement is to make men

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:50.420
much more nervous about any manifestation

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.510
of any behavior that's vaguely sexual

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:58.420
under any circumstances
what-so-ever that are

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.500
What's starting to bend
and distort company policy

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.270
NBC prohibits hugging and Netflix

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:06.090
doesn't allow you to look at anyone

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:07.610
for more than five seconds.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.680
Now really?

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.220
That's supposed to be a solution?

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.910
Who thought that through?

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:15.000
It's the suspicion of men, I would think

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.640
as men per say that's...

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.982
clearly not in anyone's interest at all.

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:26.340
So I don't wanna shock
anyone, I really don't

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.743
but the world is still run by men.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.160
And I'm just not sure
it's going that well.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:36.860
Facebook COO Sheryl Sandberg

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.983
is a leading supporter of MeToo.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.200
Even she is worried that some of

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.490
the reverberations could
prove counterproductive.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.630
I think MeToo is an opportunity.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:49.830
It's an opportunity to get rid of behavior

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.070
that never should have
happened in the first place.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.160
But we want to make sure this

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.120
doesn't have negative consequences.

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:57.980
Sandberg is a prominent advocate

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.060
for gender equality in business and the

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.660
founder of the women's
empowerment foundation, Lean In.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.400
In early 2018 a survey
conducted by Lean In

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.030
found that MeToo has had an

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:11.350
adverse effect on gender relations.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.290
You have senior managers who are male

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.640
are 3.5 times more likely to hesitate

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.070
to have a dinner with a
female junior colleague

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.690
and almost half of male managers

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:23.730
are nervous about having a one-on-one

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.393
meeting with a junior woman.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.100
You can't do work if you can't
have a one-on-one meeting.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.440
My view is, everyone should
be able to work together,

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.160
have one-on-one meetings
and behave appropriately.

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.180
But at a very minimum make access equal.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:38.600
If you don't feel
comfortable having dinner

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.573
with women don't have dinner with men.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.790
In New York one pioneering company

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.490
has come up with an innovative solution

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.673
to improve relations between
sexes in the workplace.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:55.353
There we go.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.840
That one is all set up.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:01.270
Morgan Mercer is the
founder of Vantage Point.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.260
Her company is exploiting the power

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.560
of virtual reality to train men

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.440
to see the world through women's eyes.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.090
Research shows that most men don't

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:11.814
actually have a mental
framework to reference.

00:13:11.814 --> 00:13:14.250
So most men quite literally do not

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:17.530
understand what sexual
harassment feels like.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.040
Today a team from

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.550
customer analytics firm Castora

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:24.620
will be exposed to sexual
harassment scenarios

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.823
based on real life case studies.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:33.733
Great, great, great, this
is gonna be a great year.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:39.627
Rachel, really important now
to remember it's a party.

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:41.833
So pack something fitting.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:48.100
A lot of times with sexual harassment

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:50.940
it's the build up, you
know the body language

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:53.600
and the feeling of the
elephant in the room.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.030
I just, I honestly don't
know if I wanna go anymore.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.411
What do you mean we've been
working on this for months.

00:13:59.411 --> 00:14:00.670
And what about all the after parties.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.390
Well honestly Luke, that's part of it.

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.350
James was texting me all night

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.850
asking me what I'm gonna wear.

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:09.960
So what did you guys think of it?

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:13.613
I was like shocked at how
real it actually felt.

00:14:13.613 --> 00:14:15.523
Yeah.
Yeah.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.213
They like look at you and it just like,

00:14:17.213 --> 00:14:21.460
the whole like how quickly
a seemingly non-harmful

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.160
conversation about going
out as a team or something

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:25.960
or like having fun as a team can turn

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.720
into like awkwardness and harassment.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:29.560
Like it feels it could be here.

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:31.090
Like that bench they have, I've seen it

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.250
in a million start-up offices.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.350
A man was sitting to close to a woman

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.710
and it was right next to me, right.

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.350
So I felt pretty uncomfortable.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.940
And also her reactions
to some of the comments.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.020
You can pick up on some of those cues.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.960
So the discussions that have taken place

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.530
in this past year especially,

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.590
I think people are innovating in ways

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:59.590
to facilitate better conversations,
like using technology.

00:15:00.222 --> 00:15:02.453
Stuff like this is incredibly important.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.580
Large companies, including Google

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.630
and Price Water House Coopers
have expressed interest

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.790
in using this VR technology to train

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:15.173
their workforces, as has the US Congress.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.590
It all points to an important shift.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:21.231
I think that we are at a a pivotal point

00:15:21.231 --> 00:15:23.950
in society where women's
roles are being questioned.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:28.470
We have fought for rights and now we're

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.667
fighting for equality in the workplace.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:43.420
The fallout from MeToo

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.740
has prompted some men in Western countries

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:48.400
to question traditional
notions of masculinity

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.193
and what it means to be
a man in society today.

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:58.600
In Britain former film maker David Fuller

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.360
recently founded an
alternative men's collective

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:04.713
focused on challenging conventional
forms of male behavior.

00:16:05.999 --> 00:16:07.850
Thanks for coming and can
you come in a little bit.

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:09.670
Let's make it a little bit more cozy.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:12.320
Men are being challenged
culturally right now.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.700
And I think the right response
to that is to up our game.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.930
At an arts festival in Southern England,

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.390
David is running a work
shop promoting what he sees

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:23.170
as the solution to the
issues raised by MeToo.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.540
Gender is a really hot topic right now

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.280
and a lot of the things
that we're seeing out there

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:30.324
and a lot of the anger that is being felt.

00:16:30.324 --> 00:16:33.220
I think it's towards men who
are not really showing up.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.850
To me the solution to the times is not to

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:37.600
sort of shame masculinity.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:42.600
It's to really refine healthy masculinity.

00:16:42.981 --> 00:16:45.480
David believes the key to this

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.150
is teaching men to be more open

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.920
and communicative about their feelings.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:50.260
So this whole process
that we're going through

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.320
it's about how we hold ourselves back.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.430
The argument goes

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:57.220
if more men improve their
emotional intelligence,

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:59.310
relations with women will improve.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:03.040
And this will result in greater
harmony between the sexes.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:07.699
Always compare myself to
my peers, my friends--

00:17:07.699 --> 00:17:09.410
You know I want to be responsible

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:11.930
but of course what that
means is you sacrifice

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:12.860
a lot of things in the present

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.080
cause you're always trying to make sure

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.583
the future is gonna be okay.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.920
I'm always amazed at how quickly

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.453
men open up in our workshops.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.040
In society we're supposed to be a bit

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.820
sort of tougher and that kind of stuff.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:27.280
So it's kind of to be able to let that go

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.405
and just be able to be ourselves felt

00:17:29.405 --> 00:17:31.360
in a safe environment to be however

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.260
you wanted to be not you being judged.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.270
It could be some time

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:46.180
before fringe groups like this

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:49.103
make any real noise in mainstream society.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.600
But gender roles and gender relations

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.670
are being questioned more than ever before

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:55.943
in the wake of MeToo.

00:17:58.112 --> 00:17:59.920
MeToo started as a conversation

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:02.070
about sexual harassment in the workplace.

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.960
But really it sheds light on that problem

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:07.460
and a underlying fundamental problem.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.813
The lack of power that
women have historically had.

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:14.780
This global movement

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.870
has helped expose a flaw at the heart

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:20.070
of all societies and
unleash powerful forces

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:23.633
for change that might just
kick-start efforts to fix it.

